en:
...I'll try going over there.
I started walking through the darkness toward the light.
Then the light, which had been just a dot at first, grew bigger and bigger...{p}

"Do you know the name of this tea?"
he asked, with a big smile.
"The name of this tea is......"{p}

"Eeeeeek!"
Startled by the pain, I jumped up...
"{a}, {a}...!"{p}

None of the other members were in the room.
It was just Hosoda and me, the two of us, all alone.
"Where did everyone else go...?"{p}

Just then, the door suddenly opened.
"Hello there! I'm terribly sorry to be late."
I looked toward the voice, and...?{p}

When he said that, I glanced at the table, and before I knew it, a white teacup had been set there.
Inside the cup was a blackish liquid that looked like coffee at first glance.
The grassy smell seemed to be drifting up from this cup.{p}

What, I'm in the way...?
...I wonder why.
I feel like someone said something like that to me before.{p}

When I screamed, it slid back into her mouth as if startled.
In an instant, a cold silence closed in around us.
But...{p}

"...Yeah."
Hosoda answered with a little nod.
The interview was complete...{p}

I stood still right where I was and didn't move.
...And yet the light, which had been like a dot at first, kept growing bigger and bigger.
I'm being drawn in...★{p}

...What on earth is wrong with this person's taste buds?
Whether or not he noticed me staring at him, full of suspicion and doubt...
the man just went on elegantly drinking his tea.{p}

"Me too!
I want some too...☆"
No sooner had Hosoda shouted than he tried to snatch the cup right out of my hands.{p}

The cup left my hand and in an instant was falling to the hard floor...
Crash...☆
With a grating sound, white shards and blackish liquid went flying.{p}

Back then...
Hosoda was being such a nuisance that we just left the broken cup there and went home.
That tea... most of it spilled, but a little might have been left on the shards.{p}

"Hosoda...
This is what happens when you go and lick just a little of it."
With that, Takeuchi threw the window blinds wide open.{p}

"Waah!
St-stop it, pleeease!"
On top of the wailing Hosoda's head, lush green leaves were swaying.{p}
